  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5337041/assistant-professor-instructor-of-education-the-child-the-curriculum-in-early": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Instructor of Education -The Child & The Curriculum in Early Childhood Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor/Instructor of Education -The Child & The Curriculum in Early Childhood Education Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Faculty - Part Time, Exempt, Contract based Job Number 202600052 Division Academic Affairs Department Education Dept Opening Date 05/08/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW The Department of Education at Southwestern University invites applications for a part-time Instructor/Adjunct Professor to teach The Child and the Curriculum in Early Childhood Education in Spring 2027 . This course introduces early childhood pedagogy, curriculum, and settings. Students examine typical and atypical development, play development, and culturally responsive, play-based strategies. The course emphasizes curriculum choices across content areas (math, science, art, music, theatre, PE, health) and requires students to plan, present, and evaluate lessons aligned with developmentally appropriate practice (DAP) and the Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills (TEKS). A directed observation and participation component in early childhood classrooms (up to 2 hours per week) is integral to the course. The successful candidate will be prepared to connect child development theory to instructional design, assessment, and classroom practice in early childhood contexts. QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, Curriculum & Instruction (EC), Special Education (EC), or a closely related field Ph.D./Ed.D. preferred Demonstrated teaching expertise in early childhood curriculum, DAP, play-based learning, and culturally responsive practice Experience supporting lesson design and delivery across multiple content areas in early childhood settings Familiarity with TEKS and early childhood field-based supervision/observation practices ADDITIONAL INFORMATION To apply, please submit: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for two references Sample lesson plan or syllabus excerpt demonstrating DAP + TEKS alignment (recommended) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary: $4,200 (terminal degree in-hand by January 1) or $3,900 (Master’s degree in-hand by January 1). Non-benefitted position. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Employees in this position may contribute to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan via payroll deductions. Part-time employees who complete 1,000 hours of service during their first year of employment, or during each subsequent anniversary year afterward, become eligible to receive the University’s 7% retirement contribution. Additional perks include access to athletic facilities, free parking, and reduced meal rates, along with all legally required benefits such as workers’ compensation and Social Security. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5422058/assistant-professor-of-engineering-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Engineering - Tenure-Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Engineering - Tenure-Track Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Faculty - Full Time, Tenure Track, Regular Job Number 202600070 Division Academic Affairs Department Physics and Engineering Dept Opening Date 07/23/2026 Closing Date 11/2/2026 12:00 AM Central Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Southwestern University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Engineering to begin in August 2027. Southwestern University is actively pursuing ABET accreditation for its newly launched B.S. in Engineering. The successful candidate will join a small, collaborative engineering faculty and will be expected to contribute meaningfully to program assessment, continuous improvement, and the ABET accreditation process of this general engineering degree. The University’s standard teaching load is five courses a year, along with departmental responsibilities, advising, university service, and participation in the University’s First-Year Seminar Program. Candidates will be expected to teach introductory-level physics and engineering courses as well as upper-level engineering courses. The candidate will be encouraged to develop two specialty courses in their specific area of interest. Candidates must be committed to excellence in teaching undergraduate courses and interdisciplinary collaboration. For more information regarding the Department of Physics & Engineering please visit https://www.southwestern.edu/engineering . This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must possess a Ph.D. in an engineering discipline. ABD candidates will be considered, but the degree must be completed by August 1, 2027. We welcome candidates with research programs in any engineering area that can engage undergraduate researchers. Programs aligned with advanced manufacturing (advanced CAD, rapid prototyping, etc.), systems design, and control systems are particularly encouraged. Prior experience with ABET-accredited engineering programs — as a student, faculty member, or in another capacity — is preferred but not required. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION To apply, please submit the following by November 1, 2026. A letter of interest A CV A statement of teaching philosophy and inclusive teaching practice, and a list of proposed courses A statement of the candidate’s research plan at an undergraduate-only liberal arts college Three letters of recommendation Starting annual salary for 9-month position: $80,000. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed this figure. Teaching in Southwestern University summer school provides faculty with an opportunity to supplement their income during the summer months. Tenure-track faculty typically conduct research with undergraduate students during the summer, and their income can be supplemented through competitive Southwestern Undergraduate Research with Faculty (SURF) funding. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5457733/director-of-payroll-and-tax-compliance": {
      "title": "Director of Payroll and Tax Compliance",
      "description": "Director of Payroll and Tax Compliance Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Staff - Full Time, Exempt, Regular Job Number 202600093 Division Finance & Administration Department Business Office Opening Date 08/21/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Finance & Accounting, the Director of Payroll & Tax Compliance oversees the University’s payroll operations and ensures timely and accurate tax compliance and reporting. DUTIES Supervise Payroll Coordinator and oversee the complete payroll process to include monthly payrolls, biweekly payrolls, and student payrolls. Review each payroll upon completion and finalize all payroll related payments for taxes and benefits. Prepare journal entries for the payments. Review annual payment schedules and other communications prepared by Payroll Coordinator before release. Collaborate with Payroll Coordinator, IT, and Human Resources to resolve any discrepancies as needed. Periodically reconcile payroll related liability accounts. Respond to campus personnel with payroll reports as requested. Prepare the SU 990 and 990-T tax returns and extensions. Prepare the SU Foundation 990 and 990-T tax returns, extensions, and all required forms. Review Forms K-1 from certain investments for unrelated business taxable income and prepare peripheral tax forms for international investments (Forms 926). Review the international vendor Forms W-8 series; obtaining proper authorization paperwork and filing necessary tax form such as Form 1042. Manage international student reporting and tax compliance such as Form 1042. Set up annual federal and applicable state income tax, FICA and MEDI tax withholding tables in the Datatel payroll system. Review and determine the taxable reimbursement of employee moving reimbursements. Prepare monthly state sales tax returns and payment journal entries. Prepare and reconcile the quarterly 941 and TWC reports. Prepare and remit out of Texas state income tax withholding and unemployment returns as required. Calculate annual taxable student housing wages and applicable taxes. Reconcile annual W-2’s to the quarterly 941 worksheets; work with IT to ensure all wage types and benefits are mapped to the correct boxes of the W-2. Prepare the President’s W-2 reconciliation. Prepare and file the IRS annual tax reporting forms – 1099R, 1099C, 1099M, 1099K, 1098T and W-2s. File Form 1099-NEC, 1099-MISC, and 1098-T. Pay the weekly health insurance claims invoices one approved by HR. Prepare journal entries. Prepare monthly health insurance journal entries. Prepare quarterly fixed asset acquisition and disposal journal entries. Prepare and send out annual fixed asset inventory sheets. Prepare journal entries for outside events and summer camps. Reconcile annual retirement plan contributions in connection with the 403(b) plan audit. Provide requested payroll and other information for the annual Workers’ Compensation audit. Set-up, monitor and pay any out-of-state taxes as necessary. Work with Financial aid to reconcile federal work study wages with applicable government allowances and to reconcile endowed scholarship spending for each academic year. Assist with year-end accruals and audit preparation. Additional Duties: Special projects as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Work Supervision: This position supervises the Payroll Coordinator position who processes payrolls. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum education, experience, licenses, certifications, and competencies (knowledge, skills, and behaviors) which are necessary for performing the listed duties. Bachelor’s degree. Three years of professional level experience in accounting or tax compliance. Demonstrated comprehension of IRS tax compliance for non-profit organizations. Possess strong accounting skills and knowledge of the state payroll laws. Excellent conflict resolution skills and an astute problem-solving ability. Excellent organizational skills and the ability to handle multiple tasks with a keen attention to detail. Possess basic spelling, grammar, punctuation, proofreading, and drafting skills. Ability to work both independently and as a member of a team. Ability to read, understand, and follow written and verbal instructions. Demonstrated advanced excel and word processing software skills. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to providing outstanding customer service, including outstanding telephone etiquette and listening skills. Flexibility regarding changing priorities. Possess the applications of tact, diplomacy, sensitivity, and confidentiality. Understanding and commitment to a liberal arts education, including the ability to relate to a liberal arts faculty. Ability to attend work consistently and maintain a regular work schedule. Ability to sit for extended periods of time. Ability to reach, twist, bend, stoop, stand, kneel, handle, push/pull, and lift and carry up to ten pounds. Ability to hear, see, and speak. Preferred Position Requirements: CPA License. 3+ years of professional-level accounting and tax experience. Work experience in higher education or non-profit organization. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Starting annual salary: $ 95,809. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed the starting annual salary. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5470387/assistant-professor-of-biochemistry-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biochemistry- Tenure-Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biochemistry- Tenure-Track Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Faculty - Full Time, Tenure Track, Regular Job Number 202600099 Division Academic Affairs Department Chemistry Dept Opening Date 09/02/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Southwestern University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position with expertise in biochemistry beginning in August of 2027. We seek a dedicated biochemist committed to innovative, student-centered education who is enthusiastic about mentoring undergraduates in both classroom and research settings. The successful candidate will have opportunities to contribute to the University’s developing interdisciplinary neuroscience program and general education curriculum. The successful candidate will teach five courses per academic year in our American Chemical Society (ACS) approved department. These courses will include undergraduate upper-level biochemistry lectures and laboratories, general chemistry, and specialty courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Additional responsibilities include maintaining an active scholarly agenda, academic advising, and departmental and university service. The department encourages applications from candidates with a demonstrated interest in fostering inclusive excellence in the classroom, curricular innovation, and pedagogical creativity. Additional information about the Chemistry and Biochemistry Department is available at www.southwestern.edu/chemistry-and-biochemistry/ . This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization QUALIFICATIONS PhD in in Biochemistry, Chemical Biology, Chemistry, or a closely related field within chemistry from an accredited institution. Advanced ABD candidates from an accredited university may also be considered with the expectation that the terminal degree will be earned by August 1, 2027. Strong commitment to student success and teaching at a residential liberal arts and sciences institution. Ability to establish and maintain an active research program involving undergraduate students. Postdoctoral and/or prior teaching experience is desirable but not required. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Please submit the following materials: A letter of interest detailing your qualifications, commitment to undergraduate education at a liberal arts and sciences institution, and expertise in biochemistry. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy outlining your approach to undergraduate teaching, including evidence-based and inclusive teaching practices and your experience or plans for engaging a diverse student population (no more than 2 pages). A statement of research interests and plans, including the potential for meaningful undergraduate student involvement in the proposed research program (no more than 3 pages). Contact information for three references. Supplementary materials requested at a later stage: Finalists will be asked to have letters of recommendation submitted promptly, so applicants should ensure that references are prepared to provide letters on short notice. Review of applications will begin on October 2 and continue until the position is filled. Starting annual salary for 9-month position: $70,000. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed this figure. Teaching in Southwestern University summer school provides faculty with an opportunity to supplement their income during the summer months. Tenure-track faculty typically conduct research with undergraduate students during the summer, and their income can be supplemented through competitive Southwestern Undergraduate Research with Faculty (SURF) funding. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5492952/custodian-i": {
      "title": "Custodian I",
      "description": "Custodian I Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Staff - Full Time, Hourly, Regular Job Number 202600105 Division Finance & Administration Department Facilities Management Opening Date 09/23/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Under the direction of the Manager of Custodial Services, the Custodian I performs routine cleaning and custodial duties to maintain assigned campus areas in a clean, safe, and orderly condition. DUTIES Maintain any and all buildings and assignments as assigned by the Manager of Custodial Services either directly or through a Lead Custodian. Preform duties to include, but not limited to the following: Clean, Mop, dust, vacuum, and in general maintain the cleanliness level of an assigned area. Clean lavatories, toilets, fountains, glass, mirrors, etc. Replace paper towels, tissue, soap, body soap, and trash liners as appropriate. Clean vents, fixtures, and doors; polish furniture, wood surfaces, railing, windowsills, and other surfaces. Maintain custodial supplies, equipment, and closets in a neat and organized manner and in working order. Empty and clean wastepaper receptacles inside and outside entries. Police for trash and debris outside around assigned buildings daily. Turn lights off or on and secure the building as necessary. Perform special projects such as cleaning windows, hardscape, mold remediation, and care of floors and walls. Safeguard keys and University property. ADDITIONAL DUTIES Move heavy furniture, supplies, and miscellaneous equipment as directed. Participate in Safety training program. Perform Other duties as assigned. Inspect and maintain equipment used and determine needs for repairs before and after use. Observe and report to Manager of Custodial Services and/or Lead, any and all defects, deterioration. and wear and tear on the facilities or through work order system. Could be directed to assist other departments, with approved training. QUALIFICATIONS Job related experience and skills: General knowledge of cleaning practices and the use of custodial chemicals, tools, and equipment and supplies. Possess the applications of tact, diplomacy, sensitivity, and confidentiality. Possess the characteristics of honesty and dependability. Ability to understand and willing comply with the University's safety regulations and safety related programs. Ability to exercise flexibility regarding changing priorities. Ability to follow and carry out work assignments in a timely manner. Ability to work any shift day, night, weekends, and/or holidays. Ability to work independently, without close supervision, and also as a member of a team. Ability and willingness to work longer hours and/or weekends when emergencies arise, events, and/or deadlines must be met. Ability to read. write, and follow instructions or be able to request Ora' instructions. Ability to read and understand product warning labels and directions for use of cleaning supplies and cleaning equipment or be able to request oral instructions. Ability to attend work consistently and maintain a regular work schedule. Comply with safety Programs. Physical/Mental: Ability to reach. twist, bend, stoop, stand, kneel. handle, push/pull, and lift. Ability to carry up to 50lbs. Ability to hear, see, and speak. Ability to work in all buildings or out of the doors in all weather conditions. Have knowledge, understanding, and acceptance of cultural differences and the diversity within the campus and community. Further preferred qualifications which are also desirable for performing the listed duties. Educational: High school diploma or GED. Experience and job-related skills: 3 years custodial experience *Possess a valid Texas driver's license in good standing with the Department of Motor Vehicles and record meets standards of the University's insurance carrier. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION S tarting hourly salary: $15.00 per hour. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed the starting hourly wage. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
