    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5506906/assistant-director-of-admission": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admission",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Admission Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Staff - Full Time, Exempt, Regular Job Number 202600112 Division Enrollment Services Department Admission Opening Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 12/2/2026 12:00 AM Central Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Reporting to the Director of Admission, the Assistant Director of Admission is a key member of the Admission team and Enrollment division. This role will contribute substantially to the achievement of enrollment goals and the strong overall reputation of the university in the community, state and nation. This role will be responsible for ensuring that Southwestern’s Campus Visit Experiences are second to none. Reporting to the Director of Admission, the Assistant Director will lead operational execution, follow-through with strategy, leveraging of assessment data, and continuous improvement of Southwestern’s campus visit programs for prospective students and their families. This is a high impact opportunity. The position oversees daily campus tours, large-scale open houses, admitted student days, specialized group visits, and virtual event-initiatives, and will substantially contribute leadership to student enrollment events hosted in Southwestern’s major markets. The Assistant Director directly manages student tour guides (Ambassadors) and Welcome Center staff, creating a welcoming, high-touch, and persuasive introduction to the university’s community and academic programs. DUTIES Strategic Leadership & Event Management Plan, execute, and evaluate high-volume daily campus tour operations, information sessions, and signature enrollment events (e.g., Open Houses, Admitted Student Days, VIP visits). Engage campus in offering high impact experiences by collaborating with academic departments, student affairs, athletics, and facility management to ensure excellent event delivery and broad campus support and participation. Innovate and expand virtual visit experiences, interactive webinars, and digital engagement options for prospective families unable to travel. Increase the annual number of campus visitors. Monitor guest feedback, report to leadership analytics, and leverage CRM data to continually assess and improve visit effectiveness. Use data to lean into strengths and improve weaknesses such that customer service ratings are high and evidence shows students and families are more likely to enroll after visiting. Student Leadership & Team Supervision Recruit, hire, train, schedule, and evaluate a team of 30–50 student tour guides/ambassadors and student front-desk staff. Design and implement comprehensive training curricula covering institution facts, storytelling techniques, customer service excellence, and inclusive communication. Conduct regular performance reviews and tour evaluations to maintain high presentation standards and authentic campus storytelling. Manage student payroll, scheduling software, and budget allocations for student staffing. Visitor Center Operations & Customer Experience Oversee the daily operations and aesthetic environment of the Welcome Center/Visitor Center. Provide useful suggestions for continuous improvement of the physical spaces that are key to an outstanding campus visit experience. Ensure a welcoming, accessible, and inclusive environment for visitors of all backgrounds and abilities. Manage visit registration software and CRM workflows (e.g., Slate) to handle reservations, check-ins, confirmation communications, and follow-up surveys. Respond to complex visitor inquiries and resolve escalated customer service issues promptly and professionally. Enrollment Strategy & General Admissions Serve as an active member of the admissions staff, participating in application review, prospective student counseling, and recruitment travel as needed. Present formal admissions information sessions to large groups of prospective students and families. Stay informed on higher education trends in campus visit management and student recruitment. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree. A minimum of 3 years of supervision and event planning experience in an undergraduate admission office. Availability and willingness to consistently maintain a regular work schedule. Also, enthusiastically and frequently work evenings, partial weekends, and campus visit programs, as needed. Demonstrated ability to self-manage time, activity, and spending, staying focused on goal achievement. Self-starter, who is calm under pressure, is flexible, meets deadlines, works without direct supervision, is able to multitask, problem-solve, and relate to a variety of personalities under diverse circumstances. Outstanding presentation, communication, and interaction skills (verbal and written). Excellent organization, decision-making, and problem-solving skills. Excellent computer skills, including the use of software such as Microsoft Suite, Adobe products. Demonstrated leadership skills, including a strong work ethic. Willingness to adhere to the University’s core values, particularly making “contributions to the well-being of humanity”. Have knowledge, understanding, and acceptance of cultural differences and the diversity within the campus and community. Demonstrated professional manner with all internal and external University constituencies. Proven ability to perform well in both confidential and stressful situations. Understanding of and commitment to a liberal arts education, including the ability to relate to a liberal arts faculty. Ability to maintain confidential information and files. A team player. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience working in the admission field and enrollment event planning. A strong preference for English and Spanish/bilingual fluency (verbal and written). Experience with Slate, CRM. Extensive knowledge of the University and the programs offered. Experience working with students from culturally diverse backgrounds. Work/leadership experience in higher education. Event planning in a professional capacity. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Starting annual salary: $56,341. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed the starting annual salary. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5506930/director-of-intercollegiate-athletics": {
      "title": "Director of Intercollegiate Athletics",
      "description": "Director of Intercollegiate Athletics Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Staff - Full Time, Exempt, Regular Job Number 202600116 Division Office of Advancement Department Athletics Opening Date 10/06/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Reporting to the Executive Vice President for Advancement, Athletics, & Career Services, the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics provides leadership and oversight for Southwestern University’s varsity athletics programs, including the effective management of athletics operations, facilities, programs, and staff. DUTIES Administer all aspects of a 22-sport intercollegiate NCAA Division Ill athletic program to include budgeting, staffing, compliance, and event management. Oversee all aspects of the operations of the Robertson Center, Athletic Fieldhouse, and all athletic fields. Hire, train, and supervise staff who are tasked with providing the required services of a high-performance Division Ill athletic program. Engage with campus leadership in the essential areas of academic success, retention, student life, student health, and career services. Actively support the Enrollment Management staff in the recruitment of new students. Participate in fundraising and revenue generation efforts to support enhanced opportunities for students. Be a vocal and active supporter of all campus initiatives. Positively represent the models and ideals of Southwestern University. ADDITIONAL DUTIES Serve as the institutional representative to all required NCAA and Conference committees. Serve on all on-campus committees as assigned. Assess opportunities for Non-SU related campus usage in alignment with the President's directives. Supervise the implementation of FRA courses. QUALIFICATIONS Master's Degree in Sports Management or equivalent (can substitute 10 years directly related experience for advanced degree) 5 years of progressively responsible administrative experience in a directly related field. Proven results in fundraising and revenue generation. Have knowledge, understanding, and acceptance of cultural differences and the diversity within the campus and community. Further preferred qualifications which are also desirable for performing the listed duties. 10 year’s experience in a directly related field. Proven experience in NCAA compliance management. Proven background in event management. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Starting annual salary: $145,025 . The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed the starting annual salary. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
