    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5520774/assistant-professor-of-art-sculpture-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art (Sculpture)- Tenure-Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Art (Sculpture)- Tenure-Track Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Faculty - Full Time, Tenure Track, Regular Job Number 202600115 Division Academic Affairs Department Art Dept Opening Date 10/19/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW The Department of Art and Art History at Southwestern University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Art (Sculpture) position beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will have a strong record of professional achievement and a commitment to undergraduate teaching. Applicants should be proficient in wood and metal fabrication, welding, and mold making, while also engaging with alternative practices and expanded approaches to sculpture. Interests in socially engaged practices, material studies, or digital processes are especially welcome. As a liberal arts and sciences university, Southwestern welcomes candidates who bring interdisciplinary approaches to their teaching and scholarship and are eager to collaborate with colleagues across departments and programs. The successful candidate will teach five courses per academic year. Teaching responsibilities will span introductory through advanced sculpture and include courses in the foundations program. The candidate will also teach interdisciplinary senior seminar and capstone courses as part of the department’s course rotation. The department welcomes opportunities to develop elective courses in the candidate’s areas of specialization as staffing and curriculum allow. Additional responsibilities include maintaining an active studio practice and exhibition record, academic advising, and departmental and university service. The department encourages applications from candidates with a demonstrated interest in fostering inclusive excellence in the classroom, curricular innovation, and pedagogical creativity. Additional information about the Studio Art program is available at www.southwestern.edu/art/ . The successful candidate will have a dedicated faculty office/studio of approximately 400 square feet and substantial technical support for the sculpture area. A full-time 3D technical assistant devotes half of their time to sculpture, including materials ordering, equipment and tool maintenance, budget monitoring, student worker hiring and supervision, and oversight of lab operations and safety. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization. QUALIFICATIONS MFA in Sculpture or Studio Art (sculpture emphasis) from an accredited institution An active studio practice with an exhibition record demonstrating sustained professional achievement Strong commitment to student success and teaching at a residential liberal arts and sciences institution ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Please submit the following materials by December 15, 2026 : A letter of interest Curriculum vitae Teaching philosophy addressing inclusive teaching practices Portfolio of 20 images of the candidate’s professional work Portfolio of 15 images of student work Names and contact information for three references Finalists will be asked to arrange for letters of recommendation to be submitted promptly; please ensure your references can provide them on short notice. Starting annual salary for 9-month position: $65,000. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed this figure. Teaching in Southwestern University summer school provides faculty with an opportunity to supplement their income during the summer months. Many tenure-track faculty conduct research with undergraduate students during the summer, and their income can be supplemented through competitive Southwestern Undergraduate Research with Faculty (SURF) funding. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/southwestern/jobs/5523299/part-time-instructor-assistant-professor-of-psychology-principles": {
      "title": "Part-time Instructor/Assistant Professor of Psychology (Principles)",
      "description": "Part-time Instructor/Assistant Professor of Psychology (Principles) Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Faculty - Part Time, Exempt, Contract based Job Number 202600117 Division Academic Affairs Department Psychology Dept Opening Date 10/20/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW The Psychology Department at Southwestern University seeks an instructor for one section of Principles of Psychology (introductory survey course) in Spring 2027. The section of approximately 30 students will be taught on Mondays and Wednesdays 3:30-4:45PM and must include 1-2 additional office hours on campus. The Spring semester runs from January 19 to May 5 plus final exams given the week of May 10-14. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Psychology, with a Ph.D. preferred Demonstrated teaching experience. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION To apply, please submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for two references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary: $4,200 for individuals with the terminal degree (Assistant Professor) or $3,900 for individuals with the Master’s degree (Instructor). This is a non-benefitted position. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Employees in this position may contribute to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan via payroll deductions. Part-time employees who complete 1,000 hours of service during their first year of employment, or during each subsequent anniversary year afterward, become eligible to receive the University’s 7% retirement contribution. Additional perks include access to athletic facilities, free parking, and reduced meal rates, along with all legally required benefits such as workers’ compensation and Social Security. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply"
